  "description": "Details submitted in respect of Condition 21 'Sustainable Urban Drainage Solutions (SuDS)' and  for the planning permission referenced DC/20/116403 dated 10 September 2020 for 'An application submitted under Section 73 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for minor material amendments to the planning permission DC/19/110957 dated 5 August 2019 for the erection of a building, rising to 6 storeys, comprising commercial floorspace (Use Class A1/A2/A3/B1) and 22 dwellings above, with associated landscaping, disabled and cycle parking, servicing and refuse facilities at Land at Waldram Crescent to the rear of 1-17 Stanstead Rd, London, SE23 :- in order to include a nursery (Use Class D1), \u0007 re wording of Condition(s) (2), (8), (9), (10), (11), (12), (14), (15) & (16);\u0007 Use of privacy glazing on Waldram Crescent (head to knee height rather than extending from floor to ceiling);\u0007 Access doors from the commercial unit to the garden;\u0007 Small windows added to the ground floor on the northwest elevation to provide additional daylight;\u0007 Southeast corner re-configured to provide an external entrance lobby area, covered buggy store, bin store with street access and re-allocation of commercial/visitor cycle store;\u0007 Internally, the two consented commercial units will be combined; and External landscape area to be re-allocated for commercial use'.",
